; A DEL byte (0x7F) in a payee or account still counts as -1 column when
; Ledger pads report fields, so reg keeps the layout of 3.4.1 and earlier.
;
; The payee below is "Pay", DEL, "ee" and the account "Expenses:Fo", DEL,
; "od"; the DEL bytes are invisible in most editors.  Ledger measures a
; field by the display width of its characters, and gives DEL a width
; of -1, so the 6-byte payee measures 4 columns and a 20-column field adds
; 16 spaces (the 14-byte account: 12 columns, 8 spaces).  A terminal draws
; DEL as nothing, so such a field shows one column too wide, as in 3.4.1.
; Text that is all printable ASCII is measured by its length alone, and
; DEL must not count as printable there: counted as one ordinary column,
; it would cost each field holding it two spaces and move reg's later
; columns left.  A deliberate change to the width of control characters
; (#3291) would change these lines.

2024/01/01 Payee
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

test reg
24-Jan-01 Payee                  Expenses:Food                 $10.00       $10.00
                                Assets:Cash                 $-10.00            0
end test

test reg --format '|%-20(payee)|%-20(account)|\n'
|Payee                |Expenses:Food        |
|Payee                |Assets:Cash         |
end test
